    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks, that helps. One specific issue we're running into is with lesions that have a very unusual, almost 'gnarled' or uneven texture, almost like they're protruding in small, irregular nodules. It's hard to tell if they're just complex inflammatory responses or something more structural. Is there a specific way to prioritize the coding when the texture itself is the most irregular feature, rather than just the color or location?",
