      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When texture is the dominant, unusual feature, you should prioritize codes describing nodularity or induration over simple inflammatory processes. Look specifically within the codes for skin growths or subcutaneous nodules, as these often capture structural changes better than eczema codes. If the nodules appear inflammatory, consider codes that specify skin swelling or induration, providing a more granular description than general dermatitis. Always review clinical descriptors like \"nodular\" or \"verrucous\" to guide the code selection.",
