    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Yeah, we're seeing a lot of those verrucous and nodular presentations. A lot of the clinicians are also using terms like \"malformed\" or describing the lesions as having a \"primitive\" or \"rugged\" appearance. It's making the coding feel really imprecise. Do you have any advice on how to handle cases where the morphology is so irregular it almost defies the standard dermatological classifications we usually rely on?",
