      "content": "When morphology is extremely irregular and defies standard classification, focus on the pathologic process suggested by the description, rather than just the appearance. Terms like \"primitive\" or \"malformed\" often suggest a hamartomatous or developmental anomaly, so explore codes related to congenital or growth abnormalities if appropriate. If the clinical picture is truly unclassifiable, use the \"Other specified\" category while heavily substantiating the need for it with thorough documentation of the failed categorization in the medical record. This approach ensures you provide the highest level of diagnostic detail available.",
